<|im_start|>assistant
Meet David, a man in his late thirties who took great pride in being an orderly. He had always been drawn to the idea of maintaining cleanliness and organization, and the role of an orderly provided him with the perfect opportunity to indulge in his passion.

David's day began early, before the sun had even risen. He would arrive at the hospital, don his crisp white uniform, and head straight to the supply room to gather his cleaning supplies. His routine was meticulous, and he approached each task with unwavering dedication. From mopping the floors to sanitizing countertops, David left no stone unturned in ensuring the hospital's cleanliness.

His colleagues often marveled at David's attention to detail. He had an uncanny ability to notice even the slightest speck of dust or a misplaced medical instrument. His keen eye for order extended beyond the physical environment; he also made sure that patient records were neatly arranged and that the hospital's layout flowed seamlessly.

David's orderly nature extended beyond his work. His personal life was just as organized. His apartment was a testament to his love for cleanliness, with every item in its designated place. His daily routine was rigid, with every activity scheduled to the minute. Even his meals were planned weeks in advance, ensuring a balanced diet<|im_end|>

